      "reason": "The historical-to-ssp245 change must be formed within the same member/parent variant, and the summary warns that mixing members (as for CESM2 locally) confounds forced change with internal variability.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "CESM2 historical is r1 while its ssp245 is r10 (`parent_variant_label` = historical r10i1p1f1) and the archive lacks CESM2 historical r10: no historical-to-ssp245 change can be formed for CESM2; say so on the Figure 2 panel.",
        "GFDL-ESM4 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are r1i1p1f1 in both experiments, so their 1971-2000 → 2071-2100 differences are one continuous trajectory and valid."
