      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "Comparing or ranking model OMZ fields against WOA23 and each other requires one common ocean mask over the cells all sources cover, with WOA23's land-sea mask kept out of comparisons it is not part of.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Put all fields on one grid, build one mask with `build_comparison_mask` (`ocean_only=True`, correct because WOA23 is the reference), apply `.where(mask)` to every field before any metric, and report the cell counts.",
        "Report `mean_data`/`mean_reference` returned by `compute_difference_metrics` over the shared sample, not means computed separately over each source's own cells."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "monthly-means-are-time-averages",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/monthly-means-are-time-averages.md",
      "sha256": "df6b5c23460f88f1522e5c6a665e1efbb8322c3ae876c885530f3019aa284ee0",
      "reason": "OMZ volume and thickness are nonlinear threshold diagnostics, so applying the threshold to monthly means differs from the mean of the diagnostic and the result must be stated accordingly.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "The threshold exceedance is nonlinear: choose and state the order of operations (diagnostic on each month then average, vs diagnostic of the period mean, the like-for-like choice against an observational climatology).",
        "Average the monthly fields over each period with `temporal_aggregate(freq='mean')`, which weights by calendar month length; `compute_basic_stat(op='mean', dim='time')` weights every month equally and is not a time average."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume.md",
      "sha256": "30d729792e1986dd91c822785512ceabe336ef10a47f0a7db602802e5425d70b",
      "reason": "CMIP6 o2 is stored per volume (mol m-3) while the requested thresholds and WOA23 oxygen are per mass (micromoles per kilogram), so conversion and unit care are required.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Convert model `o2` from mol m-3 to µmol kg-1 before applying the 20 and 60 thresholds: µmol kg-1 = mmol m-3 × 1000 / ρ, with in-situ ρ from `compute_potential_density_anomaly` with `ref_pressure=None` (not the `transform_unit` constant default); report `attrs['density_assumption']`.",
        "The oxygen inventory in mol needs no density: Σ o2 · volcello on the volume basis (`convert_concentration_to_content`), not from a µmol kg-1 field."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-static-grid-fields",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-static-grid-fields.md",
      "sha256": "2ad0548ca0993fa57d8f1fad27a267dcf9c0e1d007a74343d4bbdbf5b4f1ca17",
      "reason": "OMZ thickness can be recovered from volcello/areacello, and the model's own volcello/areacello/deptho are needed for volume and inventory calculations.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "OMZ volume = Σ `volcello` over cells below the threshold; column OMZ thickness = Σ `cell_thickness_like` (= volcello / areacello) over those cells. Do not take thickness from `lev_bnds` differences, which fail at partial bottom cells.",
        "`deptho` is model bathymetry (missing over land), not true topography; use it, not an external data set, to decide what is above the sea floor."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "OMZ volumes and dissolved-oxygen inventories must be volume-weighted or integrated over every ocean grid cell rather than area-averaged or subsampled.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Volume-weight every 3D mean and integral (`compute_basic_stat(op='volume_weighted_mean')`), restricting weights to cells with valid data; `compute_exceedance_fraction` does this and returns the volume (m3) behind the percentage, which belongs next to it.",
        "State the volume-weighted (Boussinesq) assumption per model; in-situ density varies only ~2 % about 1035 kg m-3."
      ]
    },
    {
